Track 1: Laserdisc Chews the Water Hyacinth
- Story & Context: When harbor bailiffs attempted to seize the produce skiffs near Tha Kha, Mae Somchit loaded a cracked optical disc into a generator-powered rig and flooded the canal with a shattering 98 BPM barrage of congas and boom-bap kicks. The smell of scorched motor oil and frying bananas mingled with the river mist as thirty grandmothers banged ironwood claves against their hulls in thunderous defiance. The bailiffs stood paralyzed by the sheer volume and infectious joy of the groove while Somchit leaned over her bow, grinning through betel-stained teeth to deliver the opening salvo: "Crack the hull wide, let the joy drown the bribe!"
