Track 3: Chok-Dee Clave Rampage
- Story & Context: By the end of the flood season, legend holds that the convergence of three rivers at Samut Songkhram was permanently locked into an endless, self-sustaining loop of cowbell syncopation and euphoric gang chants. Over two hundred merchant boats lashed themselves into a massive floating ring, passing mango sticky rice from gunwale to gunwale while trading unhinged, double-time rap verses that rattled the temple bells onshore. The police simply pulled up their folding chairs to watch, completely disarmed by the blinding communal ecstasy as the grandmothers raised their paddles in unison to chant the final anthem: "The tide belongs to the elders, bounce till the riverbanks split!"
